<title>USA: CIGNA issues $600 mln in 10- and 30-yr debt.</title>
<headline>CIGNA issues $600 mln in 10- and 30-yr debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-part debt issue from property and casualty insurance company CIGNA Corp was priced on Friday, according to lead manager Goldman, Sachs &amp; Co.</p>
<p>BORROWER CIGNA CORP</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 7.40 PCT   MATURITY 5/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.608  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD 7.456 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD 77 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>AMT $300 MLN	 COUPON 7.875 PCT  MATURITY 5/15/2027</p>
<p>TYPE DEBENTURES    ISS PRICE 99.609  FIRST PAY DATE 11/15/97</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD 7.909 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P A-MINUS   SPREAD 97 BP	CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1672))</p>
</text>
